WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.680
Customer feedback is essential to the Amazon Shopping Experience, whether positive or negative.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:15.680
For example, negative reviews can help you quickly identify and address problems with a product

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.480
listing before your business is further impacted.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.400
And product returns can reveal whether or not customers' expectations were met.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.782
Responding to customer inquiries can help reduce returns and potentially increase positive reviews

00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:34.060
by ensuring customers have the information they need before purchasing.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:40.083
To access and manage customer feedback, log in to your Amazon Seller Central account and select

00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:43.560
the menu in the top left corner of the page.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.760
Hover over the Performance tab and select Feedback Manager.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:54.487
At the top of the page, the Customer Service Insights section provides visibility into your customer

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.240
service performance.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.173
You can engage with customer inquiries through the Buyer Seller Messaging Service by clicking Go

00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:02.220
to My inbox.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:09.020
You'll also receive email notifications with a link to review and respond to customer inquiries.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:15.844
Keep in mind that questions and your responses will be visible on the product page for other shoppers

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:16.540
to reference.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.626
The Feedback Manager section allows you to track and manage buyer satisfaction metrics such as your

00:01:23.626 --> 00:01:27.420
feedback rating and view detailed feedback entries from customers.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.620
Under Recent Feedback, you'll see all reviews and their ratings from the last year.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:40.180
We recommend filtering reviews by the lowest ratings to see what's having the biggest impact on

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.980
customers and addressing those first.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:49.040
To respond to a customer review, you can select Post a Public Reply under the Actions drop-down.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:56.545
You can also visit the Voice of the Customer Dashboard for a deeper dive on customer feedback, customer

00:01:56.545 --> 00:02:02.383
experiences, health metrics and information on emerging product and listing issues across all your

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:02.800
offers.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:10.044
To access the dashboard, select the menu from the top left corner of Seller Central, hover over

00:02:10.044 --> 00:02:13.020
Performance and click on Voice of the Customer.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.833
Review the CX Health Breakdown of your Listings section to identify offers that need attention in

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:20.560
your subcategory.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:28.587
Under Offer Listings, click the See Details button under Action to access the details for a specific

00:02:28.587 --> 00:02:29.000
ASIN.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:36.266
Look for the Return Reason Code Breakdown and corresponding Customer Feedback for the previous 30

00:02:36.266 --> 00:02:36.720
days.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.300
Customer Feedback includes Return Comments and Product Reviews.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.260
You can also look for trends within the Return Reason Code Distribution.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.672
For example, if the Return Reason Code Distribution between too small and too large has a big imbalance,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.520
your sizing might be incorrect.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:03:01.120
For more information, you can watch the Voice of the Customer Overview video in Seller University.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:07.560
To manage your customer returns, select the menu in the top left corner of the Seller Central Dashboard,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.840
hover over the Orders tab and click on Manage Returns.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:19.644
At the top of the page, you'll see four quick access links to resources, such as more information

00:03:19.644 --> 00:03:25.280
on managing returns, FAQs, reports on return activity and editing your return settings.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:32.756
The main table displays all of your recent return requests with details like order number, product,

00:03:32.756 --> 00:03:34.780
return reason, and return status.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:43.014
You can use the search bar to find specific return requests by order ID, return merchandise authorization,

00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:45.920
RMA number, tracking ID, or ASIN.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:52.520
The filters let you narrow down the return requests by created date, date range, or marketplace.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:58.841
You can switch between different return request views to either see all returns, pending returns

00:03:58.841 --> 00:04:04.320
to be actioned, completed returns, or requests with an A to Z claims.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:10.747
For each return request, you can take different actions, such as authorizing the return, issuing

00:04:10.747 --> 00:04:15.460
a refund, marking the refund complete, or contacting the buyer directly.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:21.220
We recommend that you respond to any incoming return requests within 24 hours.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:28.920
We also recommend regularly reviewing your returns performance dashboard to identify areas for improvement.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.300
Click the View Returns Performance link to monitor your returns performance dashboard.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:40.821
Ensure your returns metrics stay below the stated thresholds to help guarantee a positive return

00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:42.560
experience for your buyers.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:48.740
For more best practices for handling feedback from customers, read through the Managing Your Seller

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.800
Feedback Guide in Seller University.
